    "statement": "∀ {E : Type u_1}\n  {F : Type u_2} [inst : MetricSpace E] [CompleteSpace E] [SecondCountableTopology E] [inst_3 : MeasurableSpace E]\n  [BorelSpace E] [inst_5 : MetricSpace F] [CompleteSpace F] [SecondCountableTopology F] [inst_8 : MeasurableSpace F]\n  [BorelSpace F] (μ : MeasureTheory.Measure E) (ν : MeasureTheory.Measure F) [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure μ]\n  [MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure ν] (c : E × F → NNReal),\n  Continuous c →\n    ∃ γ,\n      MeasureTheory.IsProbabilityMeasure γ ∧\n        AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.Transport.IsCoupling γ μ ν ∧\n          ∫⁻ (z : E × F), ↑(c z) ∂γ =\n            AutoSamplingTheory.TechnicalLemmas.Measure.Transport.transportCost (fun z => ↑(c z)) μ ν",
    "statement_sha256": "8fd746e059264a3f8a17abf8f564d2dcbc343db66dd8782276909f58387662dc",
    "compiled": true,
    "approved_definition_context": [
      "MetricSpace, CompleteSpace and SecondCountableTopology give complete second-countable metric spaces; BorelSpace identifies the measurable structure with the Borel sigma algebra. NormedAddCommGroup is an additive commutative group with a norm and its metric, not necessarily a vector space.",
      "IsProbabilityMeasure means total mass one. Measure.map is the pushforward of a measure by the specified map. Measure.fst and Measure.snd are pushforwards by product projections. Transport.IsCoupling gamma P Q means gamma.fst=P and gamma.snd=Q.",
      "Transport.transportCost c P Q is the infimum in extended nonnegative reals of integrals of c over all raw measures with those two marginals. It does not assume an optimizer or bounded/finite cost.",
      "NNReal are nonnegative finite reals; ENNReal are extended nonnegative reals. The displayed casts preserve nonnegative values. ENNReal.ofReal takes the nonnegative part of a real number. Lintegral is the extended nonnegative integral.",
      "Measure.real B is the real-valued measure of B, i.e. the extended measure converted to real; here all relevant measures are probabilities. A.e. refers to almost everywhere under the specified measure.",
      "Real powers are powers with real exponents. All p,r,delta quantifiers and restrictions are exactly those displayed. Norm is the norm of the actual group difference. Lets are abbreviations for the explicit maps and radius."
    ]
  },
